StyleSmuggler deferred-directives fix, magento/module-email half

One half of patches/stylesmuggler-deferred-directives-fix-247-248-249.patch. The combined patch touches two
packages, which a plugin that patches per package cannot handle, so it is split
here. Paths are left as vendor/magento/..., which those plugins resolve through
their -p4 fallback.

Package : magento/module-email
Magento : 2.4.7, 2.4.8 and 2.4.9, every patch level
Origin  : https://gist.github.com/pingiun/00cfbfdc3cf517807eb3b6bc24c7f295

Both halves are required; applying only one leaves the fix incomplete.

diff --git a/vendor/magento/module-email/Model/Template/Filter.php b/vendor/magento/module-email/Model/Template/Filter.php
index f86deacad3b..e257a38932a 100644
--- a/vendor/magento/module-email/Model/Template/Filter.php
+++ b/vendor/magento/module-email/Model/Template/Filter.php
@@ -980,6 +980,7 @@ class Filter extends Template
         // If this template is a child of another template, skip processing so that the parent template will process
         // this directive. This is important as CSS inlining must operate on the entire HTML document.
         if ($this->isChildTemplate()) {
+            $this->deferToParent($construction[0]);
             return $construction[0];
         }
 
